; Merged into the VSSDK-generated pkgdef (see <VsixPkgDefFile> in the .csproj).
;
; GeneratePkgDefFile auto-registers only assemblies marked ForceIncludeInVSIX (the
; Community.VisualStudio.Toolkit package). The Core project ships via IncludeInVSIX on the
; ProjectReference, so VSSDK does NOT emit a codeBase entry for it. Without this entry the
; net48 host (devenv.exe) resolves "Kaeo LLM Proxy VS Extension.Core" only by happenstance
; of the extension folder being on the probing path; a partial deployment then fails with
; "Could not load file or assembly" at the first send (MeaiAdapter's first type load).
; Pinning the codeBase makes that resolution deterministic.
[$RootKey$\RuntimeConfiguration\dependentAssembly\codeBase\{KAEoCorePkgDefSection-0000-0000-0000-000000000001}]
"name"="Kaeo LLM Proxy VS Extension.Core"
"publicKeyToken"=""
"culture"="neutral"
"version"="0.1.0.0"
"codeBase"="$PackageFolder$\Kaeo LLM Proxy VS Extension.Core.dll"
